. *Compute average means, e.g. mean_diff_chore is the annual average of the dif
> ference in time spent on household chores between partners within couples, ca
> lculated for each survey year (syear). It serves as a benchmark to capture th
> e average trend for each year.
. egen mean_diff_chore = mean(diff_chores), by(syear)

. egen mean_diff_childcare = mean(diff_childcare), by(syear)

. 
. *The variable perf represents the individual couple's difference relative to 
> this annual average. In other words, perf2 shows whether a given couple's gap
>  in chore time is above or below the average observed that year.
. gen perf=diff_childcare-mean_diff_childcare
